abstract: "Dirichlet Weight Regularization (dreg) — a continuous 2D Dirichlet harmonic energy penalty that breaks permutation symmetry, concentrates DCT spectral energy, and enables sub-1.0 bpp Base-3 trit quantization with <1 MB SRAM streaming via a zero-copy DMA micro-kernel. Validated on TinyStories-10M (72% roughness reduction, 7.25 PPL gain at 0.945 bpp) and MNIST MLP (+11% low-pass retention)."
